Archive : combining multiple files and directories into a single file
used in Backup/compressing data

tar --> tape archive --> linux system admins to compress data
gzip, bz2, xz  (compression methods)

#tar <options> <files>

c -> create
x -> extract
v -> verbose (means detailed)

f -> file
t -> list archive contents
z -> gzip
j -> bz2
J -> xz

create a tar archive file
tar [options] archive_name files
# tar -cvf /mnt/backup.tar /var

extract a file
#tar -xvf /mnt/backup.tar

extract a tar to a specific location
#tar -xvf /mnt/backup.tar -C /root/Desktop(space bw C and path)

compress
#tar -cvzf /mnt/backup.tar.gz /var
cvf me z before f for gzip compression, and filename me bhi gz rakhenge followed by contents

to show file size in human format
#du -sh /var
#du -sh /mnt/backup.tar


