crontab vs crond 
crond --> is the bg service(daemon)
crontab ---> file or command in which we define jobs

#systemctl start crond 
#crontab -e (set cron jobs)
syntax : Minute Hour Day-of-Month Month Day-of-Week Command
eg: 0 2 * * * tar -czf /backup.tar.gz /var/www  (creates a compressed backup at 2 AM everyday)

#crontab -l --> list all cron jobs 
#crontab -r --> remove all jobs



Linux --> file system
/bin -> user binaries -> binary executable files
/sbin -> system binaries -> fdisk,reboot,etc.
/dev -> device files -> pendrive files, or any external devices etc.

/var --> log files
/var/tmp --> temporary files

/mnt -> mount directory --> a temporary mount point for storage devices or filesystems.
can't access the external storage device through /dev, have to mount it first and then access it in /mnt

